<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	19.30	    + 99	    18.30     19.90</p>
<p>91-Day	21.31	    + 53	    21.20     21.40</p>
<p>182-Day     21.99	    + 21	    21.88     22.04</p>
<p>364-Day     22.92</p>
<p>Last week the 364-day paper was assigned at 22.99 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	600 million pesos   1.98 bln pesos     3.31</p>
<p>91-Day	600 million pesos   3.49 bln pesos     5.82</p>
<p>182-Day     600 million pesos   3.28 bln pesos     5.47</p>
<p>364-Day     800 million pesos   1.79 bln pesos     2.24</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.52 on demand of 10.55 billion pesos compared with 4.23 the week before, on demand of 12.7 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   60 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    9 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			   5 basis points</p>
<p>    364-Day			   8 basis points</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
